{"type":"item.completed","item":{"id":"item_61","type":"command_execution","command":"/bin/zsh -lc \"sed -n '1690,1743p' src/cljc/yin/vm/engine.cljc; rg -n 'defn grant|defn lower|defn lift|:accept' test/yin/vm/ucf/rows_support.cljc | tail -18; sed -n '125,162p' test/yin/vm/ucf/rows_custody_test.cljc; rg -n 'defn .*transaction|defn .*step|probe' test/yin/vm/engine_test.cljc | tail -15\"","aggregated_output":"   stream call. Refused as `apply-link-cursor` is, and for an entry\n   without `:cursor`: the cursor precedes the append.\"\n  [state link-id]\n  (let [i (link-entry-slot state link-id :link-request)]\n    (when-not (contains? (get-in state [:wait-set i]) :cursor)\n      (fail \"Link request sent before its cursor\" {:link-id link-id}))\n    (update-in state\n               [:wait-set i]\n               #(-> % (dissoc :envelope) (assoc :reason :link-response)))))\n\n\n(defn apply-link-read\n  \"Apply one read `outcome` of the link response stream to the gated\n   `:link-response` entry `link-id`, as `poll-link-response` applies one\n   read; the successor position is inside the outcome. Another id's\n   response advances the cursor and is skipped, `blocked` keeps waiting,\n   the entry's own response settles and the rest refuse. Performs no\n   stream call. Refused as `apply-link-cursor` is.\"\n  [state link-id outcome]\n  (let [i (link-entry-slot state link-id :link-response)\n        entry (get-in state [:wait-set i])\n        [_tag state' waiting woken] (link-read-step state entry outcome)\n        ws (:wait-set state')]\n    (-> state'\n        (assoc :wait-set (if waiting\n                           (assoc ws i waiting)\n                           (into (subvec ws 0 i) (subvec ws (inc i)))))\n        (update :ready-queue (fnil into []) (when woken [woken])))))\n\n\n(defn abandon-link\n  \"A composition gives up on link `link-id` (section 7.2, step 7): the\n   entry leaves the wait set and receives loss data for try-require or\n   an effect error for require; the id is retired, so a later response is\n   `:late`. The linker side's `abandon` is the composition's call. An id\n   no entry holds leaves the state unchanged.\"\n  [state link-id reason]\n  (let [held? (fn [e]\n                (and (contains? #{:link-request :link-response} (:reason e))\n                     (= link-id (:link-id e))))]\n    (if-let [entry (first (filter held? (:wait-set state)))]\n      (-> state\n          (update :wait-set (fn [ws] (filterv (complement held?) ws)))\n          (retire link-id :abandoned)\n          (update :ready-queue (fnil conj [])\n                  (refused-entry entry\n                                 {:status :lost,\n                                  :reason reason,\n                                  :link-id link-id})))\n      state)))\n\n\n(defn abandon-installs\n  \"A composition gives up on every install in flight (the abandoned case\n359:(defn lift-opts\n366:(defn lift\n\n\n(defn- refused\n  \"The refusal of wire lowered under opts, asserting zero attachments.\"\n  [wire opts]\n  (let [[r n] (lowered wire opts)]\n    (is (zero? n) (str \"refused before any attachment: \" (pr-str (select-keys r [:yin.k/status :yin.k/kind]))))\n    r))\n\n\n(def ^:private successor (delay (f/base \"successor\")))\n\n\n(deftest an-exclusive-root-lowers-under-its-grant\n  (let [wire @successor\n        [m n] (lowered wire (exclusive-opts wire #{\"s0\"}))]\n    (is (pos? n))\n    (is (= {:yin.k/occurrence s/occurrence :dao.lease/lease \"lease-1\" :dao.lease/holder \"holder-a\"\n            :yin.k/epoch 0 :yin.k/arbitration s/arbitration :yin.k/next-op-seq 3\n            :protection {\"s0\" :enrolled}\n            :input {:next 0 :prefix (get-in (grant-for wire #{\"s0\"}) [:evidence :yin.k/prefix])}\n            :tenure {:bound 10}}\n           (:yin.k/custody m))\n        \"custody from the evidence, the counter the slot's exactly\")\n    (is (= :running (:yin.k/gate m)))\n    (is (= 1 (:yin.k/issued m)))\n    (let [put (first (filter #(= :put (:reason %)) (:wait-set m)))]\n      (is (= 0 (:yin.k/issue put)) \"retained writes are numbered in carried order\")\n      (is (= (s/op-id 0) (:op-id put)) \"the id travels verbatim\"))\n    (testing \"the restored task relifts to the same root under the same header\"\n      (is (= (:yin.k/root wire)\n             (:yin.k/root (rows/lift-task (dissoc m :yin.k/custody :yin.k/gate :yin.k/issued) (s/serve-table)\n                                          (s/lift-opts (s/header 3 s/origin #{\"s0\"})))))))))\n\n\n(deftest the-counter-is-restored-exactly\n  (doseq [k [0 3 7 (dec rows/max-exact)]]\n    (let [wire (f/edit-custody @successor #(assoc % :yin.k/next-op-seq (inc k)))\n462:          bad {:reason :stare, :k {:type :probe-frame}, :env {}}\n482:               :k {:type :probe-frame},\n577:                                    :k {:type :probe-frame},\n633:                                    :k {:type :probe-frame},\n823:                                                    {:key :probe, :val 42})\n836:                                         {:k {:type :probe-frame}, :env {}})\n","exit_code":0,"status":"completed"}}
