ions are\n27:slice (§4.3), the live operand subtracts the virtual destination before\n49:that §§4.1-4.3, 5.2, 5.3, 5.5, 5.6, 6.3, 7, 8.3, 8.5, 9 state what\n124:   layouts (frozen §4.3, §10 phase 6).\n257:The two delivery states of §1.1 are the states at which the evaluator parks by itself. They are special cases of its general state between any two instructions, `⟨A, pc, W↾L(pc), E, K⟩`, which `vm-hot` materializes whenever fuel runs out (`semantic.cljc:142-143`) and which the carrier expresses as the `run` state of §1.2. A step is atomic: effects are observed only inside a step or inside the scheduler's sweep, so no state between steps holds a half-issued effect; atomicity of a step is not transactionality of the outside world (an append performed before a host exception is not undone). A task is a **product**: at most one active activation (the `run`), its ordered pending waits, its ordered completed wakes (the ready queue: a woken wait with the value, status and cursor update its effect produced, carried by the `:ready` row of §2.3), its parked table, and its stores. The scheduler constructs every combination: resuming one of several woken waits leaves the others queued and the unresolved ones pending (`engine.cljc:2294-2312`, `:2305`). Every such state is **representable**. The lift refuses only what is not **portable** (a value with no wire form), not **satisfied** (code or dependencies the receiver lacks), or a **hold** (a driver-internal observation in flight: §7.1 step 1), never a pc. The static correspondence of §4 holds at every pc of a body: distinct virtuals in `L(p) ∪ def(p)` hold distinct physical registers (`derive/allocation`), and the stack kernel's operand region at A pc `p` is `stack-layout(p) ++ uses(p)` above a dead prefix (§4.3); both are checks (§5.6), not theorems. A root whose task has an active activation has kind `:running` (§2.6) and is a custody subject like a blocked or parked root (§7.3).\n354:**DECIDED** (draft §5.3, UCF §7.4.3, v2 amendment §2): one kind\n636:**DECIDED** (frozen §4.3; UCF §7.4.2). A foreign engine publishes a\n708:dispatch in one place; the algorithms of §4.2-4.3 are unchanged.\n849:### 4.3 The stack kernel's layout\n886:Let `register-sequence(p) = layout(p) ++ uses-in-order(p)` and `expected-values(p) = [W[r] for r in register-sequence(p)]`. Compare ordered region length and contents to that sequence, including repeated-register agreement. Separately check `set(layout(p)) ∪ set(uses(p)) = L(p)` at reachable non-tail PCs and `set(uses(p)) = L(p)` at reachable tail-call PCs. Ordered multiplicity is not the cardinality of `L(p)`. Retain the parked-window check. The dead-prefix treatment and running backend lift belong to 6e.\n1146:5. **Retained FFI across a de Bruijn receiver** (§4.3, 6c Q2\n1158:**Cross-references.** Frozen design §4.3 and §10 phases 5, 6 and 8;\n1287:| 20 | **tail-effect halt** | run **outside the wrappers**, in two batches on one machine: a setup batch `(then (def! 's (stream/make 4)) (def! 'c (cursor-of s)))` run to halt (store writes persist across batches, as `lift_support.cljc:320-322` relies on), then the batch `(stream/next! c)` **marked `:tail? true` at the root**, `c` resolving through the store; no application precedes the call, so `K` is empty (any `let1` or wrapper would push a frame, §5.2 above) | append `\"B\"` | tail, `:next` | halts with `\"B\"` (4b: a tail effect with no frame to pop halts, `srvm-phase4b:semantic_register.cljc:205-211` stage 2; stack: the seam's empty-`K` case, §4.3), env free of `store-of` | yes |\n1360:9, 12, 20) require the seam of §4.3 and are gated on 6c-pre.\n1392:and the retained-FFI re-park is a kernel edit (§4.3); 2-3 days of\n1525:   `m+1` slices of §4.3 partition the stack kernel's operand stack\n2240:`src/cljc/yin/vm/debruijn/stack.cljc` (§4.3): park-entry builders mark a\n2301:   lowering the lifted frame emits the same five bases (§4.3; the\n2414:kernels (§4.3, 6c-post-D2), was rejected by the owner (§11, 6c Q2); this\n2420:#**Dead ambient operands (static domain).** The non-tail set equation holds where the enclosing application's pending reads are still reachable. At the operand PCs of an application whose evaluation an operand-position tail call or `:resume` abandons (the corpus's `:resume-operand` and `:tail-operand` fixtures), ambient layout entries are dead per L while remaining in the region: the strongest static truth there is the inclusion `uses(p) ⊆ L(p) ⊆ layout(p) ∪ uses(p)`; the equality is permanently excluded at those pcs. 6e's dead-prefix rule governs the region after the transfer, and 6e's ordered dynamic checks — not the static set equality — carry those pcs.\n48:            (is (= expected (layout/lower-defect task lane)))\n58:          (is (nil? (layout/lower-defect (rows/decode wire rows/default-budget) lane))))))\n","exit_code":0,"status":"completed"}}
