envelope is never reconstructed or appended\"))))\n  2567\t\n  2568\t\n  2569\t(deftest completion-outcome-slot-matrix\n  2570\t  (doseq [prepare [#(let [[m src] (parked-reader)]\n  2571\t                     (stream/append! src \"B\") (engine/check-wait-set m))\n  2572\t                   #(let [[m out id] (two-callers)] (answer-both! out id) (engine/check-wait-set m))\n  2573\t                   #(let [world (writer identity)] ((first (:steps world))) (engine/check-wait-set (:machine world)))\n  2574\t                   #(let [world (retained-ffi identity)] ((first (:steps world))) (engine/check-wait-set (:machine world)))\n  2575\t                   #(let [m (:machine (linking identity false true))]\n  2576\t                      (engine/abandon-link m (:link-id (first (:wait-set m))) :gone))\n  2577\t                   #(let [m (:machine (linking identity false false))]\n  2578\t                      (engine/abandon-link m (:link-id (first (:wait-set m))) :gone))\n(defn- step1\n  \"Execute exactly one instruction and return the resulting VM. Assumes the\n   VM's continuation is active; callers (`step`, `run`) check that first.\"\n  [vm]\n  (let [{:keys [segment pc frames free-env stack continuation\n                primitives modules store-of]}\n        vm\n        inst (nth segment pc)\n        op (nth inst 0)]\n    (case op\n      :const\n      (assoc vm :pc (inc pc) :stack (conj stack (nth inst 1)))\n\n      :load-bound\n      (let [depth (nth inst 1), position (nth inst 2)]\n        (assoc vm\n               :pc (inc pc)\n               :stack (conj stack (frame-value frames depth position))))\n\n      :load-free\n      (let [name (nth inst 1)\n            value (engine/resolve-var free-env\n                                      (engine/active-store vm store-of)\n                                      primitives modules name)]\n        (assoc vm :pc (inc pc) :stack (conj stack value)))\n\n      ;; This positional dimension has no `:macro?` flag on `:closure` (it\n      ;; is named-datom-only, section 4): the instruction carries only\n      ;; arity and a body pc, so there is nothing here to ignore.\n      :closure\n      (let [arity (nth inst 1), body-pc (nth inst 2)]\n        (assoc vm\n               :pc (inc pc)\n               :stack (conj stack\n                            (values/closure\n                              (:owner vm)\n                              (cond-> {:type :closure, :arity arity,\n                                       :body-pc body-pc, :frames frames}\n                                store-of (assoc :store-of store-of))))))\n\n      ;; Every value-producing opcode puts its result directly onto :stack.\n      ;; The retained :push instruction therefore only advances pc: its value\n4. **Completed link/install outcomes.** Exercise success, try failure and ordinary raised failure for link/install producers. Capture completed install outcomes after removal of the install entry. Include active control beside a remaining completion. Immediate relift is equal; continuation delivers or raises once, without reconstructing retired pending resources.\n\n5. **Shared cursor.** Two waiters share one cursor. Snapshot after the sweep before any resume. Preserve one canonical cell identity, the slot-9 current body, both values and update rows in order. Assert immediate relift equality and source/receiver continuation equality. Add an encoding case where one C pairs with different bodies across census/update rows.\n\n6. **Completed write and terminal outcomes.** Fork and exclusive completed-write histories round-trip without enrollment or reappend. A malformed present ID refuses at the named slot-18 check. Nil IDs remain admissible where the ungated source produced none. Add a terminal-status ready case whose receiver raises identically, plus the FFI sent-request transition that creates a response wait without a second request append.\n\n7. **Every returned boundary, slow tier.** Run the existing corpus through `run-fuel 1`; lift, lower into isolated worlds, immediately relift, validate frames and continue to the reference outcome. Pin measured counts and the driver coverage classes of §3.6. Constructed post-sweep cases are reported separately. Row 20's setup batch (`s/def!` store definitions executed at runtime) lifts only from the first boundary at which its definitions are answered in the store; the leading boundary is excluded as a **pinned conservative-discharge false refusal of the owner-ratified Q6 family (default 5: keep edge-reachability, derive don't persist)** — recorded per case with its obligations and zero serves, never skipped silently: the driver asserts the excluded boundaries form a contiguous leading run and that every boundary after the first successful lift lifts.\n\n8. **Quick sample and products.** Retain v2’s structural sample and every-boundary small rows. Run the scheduler products and shared-cursor seam through the harness. Retain cursor-ref, reified-continuation, nil-live-register, `ghost` and hold-refusal cases.\n\n9. **Layout gates.** At every reachable corpus PC, check register injectivity and jump/terminator layout availability; at every reachable tail-call PC check `set(uses(p)) = L(p)`; at every other reachable PC check the inclusion `set(uses(p)) ⊆ L(p) ⊆ set(layout(p)) ∪ set(uses(p))`, and additionally the equality `set(layout(p)) ∪ set(uses(p)) = L(p)` everywhere **except the pinned dead-ambient operand PCs — exactly `{(:resume-operand 1), (:resume-operand 2), (:tail-operand 1), (:tail-operand 2)}`** — where an operand-position `:resume` (abortive) or tail call (the enclosing application's call is unreachable) makes the enclosing application's pushed operands dead per L while they remain in the static layout and on the stack. At the pinned PCs assert the exclusion's cause: the layout entries outside `L(p)` are exactly those dead ambient operands. The exclusion set is enumerated, never predicate-based: a future corpus entry with a dead ambient layout fails the equality loudly rather than being skipped. On executed paths compare ordered region length and values to the ordered register sequence, including repeated-register agreement. Do not compare that sequence length to `|L(pc)|`. No dead-prefix lift, `slice-window` widening, or running-backend lift is implemented in 6d-a; those remain 6e item 6's scope.\n(require '[clojure.test :as t]\n         'yin.vm.semantic.frame-test\n         'yin.vm.semantic.vm-test\n         'yin.vm.engine-test\n         'yin.vm.ucf.rows-test\n         'yin.vm.semantic.safepoint-harness-test\n         'yin.vm.semantic.layout-test)\n(doseq [sym '[yin.vm.semantic.frame-test/run-state-rules\n              yin.vm.semantic.vm-test/fuel-and-closed-gates\n              yin.vm.semantic.vm-test/bounded-bridge-calls-return\n              yin.vm.semantic.vm-test/fuel-dispatch-and-diagnostic-bridge-are-bounded\n              yin.vm.engine-test/budgeted-install-children\n              yin.vm.ucf.rows-test/running-task-round-trip-and-fencing\n              yin.vm.ucf.rows-test/run-row-slot-and-reference-kinds\n              yin.vm.semantic.safepoint-harness-test/a-nonempty-ready-queue-is-carried\n              yin.vm.semantic.safepoint-harness-test/completed-link-and-install-outcomes\n              yin.vm.semantic.safepoint-harness-test/task-products-and-ready-validation\n              yin.vm.semantic.safepoint-harness-test/completed-put-history-and-shape-only-ids\n              yin.vm.semantic.safepoint-harness-test/ready-value-portability-and-independent-update-body\n              yin.vm.semantic.safepoint-harness-test/halted-with-outstanding-waits-is-normalized-separately\n              yin.vm.semantic.safepoint-harness-test/completion-try-and-update-refusals\n              yin.vm.semantic.safepoint-harness-test/completed-ffi-append-becomes-a-response-wait\n              yin.vm.semantic.safepoint-harness-test/terminal-completed-write-raises-the-same-outcome\n              yin.vm.semantic.safepoint-harness-test/ready-site-mismatch-and-halted-product\n              yin.vm.semantic.safepoint-harness-test/pre-branch-ghost-is-conservatively-unsatisfied\n              yin.vm.semantic.safepoint-harness-test/sampled-returned-boundaries\n              yin.vm.semantic.layout-test/static-layouts-at-every-pc]]\n  (binding [t/*report-counters* (ref t/*initial-report-counters*)]\n    (t/test-vars [(resolve sym)])\n    (println \"ACCEPTANCE-VAR\" sym (pr-str @t/*report-counters*))))\n","exit_code":0,"status":"completed"}}
