{"type":"item.completed","item":{"id":"item_117","type":"command_execution","command":"/bin/zsh -lc \"head -34 src/cljc/yin/vm/semantic/frame.cljc; rg -n 'defn- (bad\"'!|custody-refuse!|outcome!)'\"' src/cljc/yin/vm/ucf/rows.cljc; tail -4 target/6da/r2-focused-b.log; rg -n '\"'^FAIL|''^ERROR|actual:'\"' target/6da/r2-focused-b.log | head -16; rg -n 'frames restore|running.*blocked|Quiesce|not-quiescent|:ready-reason' docs/design/yin.vm.semantic.continuation.md docs/design/yin.vm.ucf-transport-tuples.md docs/design/yin.vm.semantic.md docs/design/yin.vm.universal-continuation-format.md | head -32\"","aggregated_output":"(ns yin.vm.semantic.frame\n  \"Pure, ordered validation of decoded canonical continuation frames (§3).\"\n  (:require [dao.jing.cbor :as cbor]\n            [yin.vm :as vm]\n            [yin.vm.values :as values]\n            [yin.vm.semantic.code :as code]\n            [yin.vm.semantic.analysis :as analysis]))\n\n\n(defn- problem\n  [kind path]\n  {:yin.k/kind kind :yin.k/path path})\n\n\n(defn- closed?\n  [x required optional]\n  (and (map? x) (every? #(contains? x %) required)\n       (every? (into (set required) optional) (keys x))))\n\n\n(defn task-defect\n  \"X1, once per body, including a halted body with no frames.\"\n  [task]\n  (let [e (:free-env task)]\n    (cond\n      (not (and (map? e) (every? symbol? (keys e))))\n      (problem :free-env-shape [:free-env])\n      (some vm/reserved-name? (keys e))\n      (problem :reserved-name [:free-env]))))\n\n\n(defn- env?\n  [e]\n  (and (closed? e [:yin.k/bindings] [:yin.k/store-of])\n98:(defn- bad!\n1225:(defn- custody-refuse!\n1387:(defn- outcome!\n\nTesting yin.vm.semantic.frame-test\n\nTesting yin.vm.semantic.safepoint-harness-test\ndocs/design/yin.vm.ucf-transport-tuples.md:478:| root | running / blocked / parked | exclusive | `{:yin.k/policy :yin.k/exclusive :yin.k/occurrence :yin.k/arbitration :yin.k/next-op-seq}` plus `:yin.k/origin` on every successor, absent on a first export |\ndocs/design/yin.vm.ucf-transport-tuples.md:479:| root | running / blocked / parked | fork | nil |\ndocs/design/yin.vm.universal-continuation-format.md:1673:  (`:yin.k/not-quiescent` otherwise, §7.4.1) — a task with queued runnable\ndocs/design/yin.vm.universal-continuation-format.md:1900:1. **Quiesce**: the ready-queue must be empty (§7.6.3).\ndocs/design/yin.vm.universal-continuation-format.md:2628:   ready-queue is empty, else `:yin.k/not-quiescent`.\ndocs/design/yin.vm.universal-continuation-format.md:3136:  `:yin.k/not-at-safepoint`; queued work gives `:yin.k/not-quiescent`.\ndocs/design/yin.vm.semantic.continuation.md:257:The two delivery states of §1.1 are the states at which the evaluator parks by itself. They are special cases of its general state between any two instructions, `⟨A, pc, W↾L(pc), E, K⟩`, which `vm-hot` materializes whenever fuel runs out (`semantic.cljc:142-143`) and which the carrier expresses as the `run` state of §1.2. A step is atomic: effects are observed only inside a step or inside the scheduler's sweep, so no state between steps holds a half-issued effect; atomicity of a step is not transactionality of the outside world (an append performed before a host exception is not undone). A task is a **product**: at most one active activation (the `run`), its ordered pending waits, its ordered completed wakes (the ready queue: a woken wait with the value, status and cursor update its effect produced, carried by the `:ready` row of §2.3), its parked table, and its stores. The scheduler constructs every combination: resuming one of several woken waits leaves the others queued and the unresolved ones pending (`engine.cljc:2294-2312`, `:2305`). Every such state is **representable**. The lift refuses only what is not **portable** (a value with no wire form), not **satisfied** (code or dependencies the receiver lacks), or a **hold** (a driver-internal observation in flight: §7.1 step 1), never a pc. The static correspondence of §4 holds at every pc of a body: distinct virtuals in `L(p) ∪ def(p)` hold distinct physical registers (`derive/allocation`), and the stack kernel's operand region at A pc `p` is `stack-layout(p) ++ uses(p)` above a dead prefix (§4.3); both are checks (§5.6), not theorems. A root whose task has an active activation has kind `:running` (§2.6) and is a custody subject like a blocked or parked root (§7.3).\ndocs/design/yin.vm.semantic.continuation.md:420:   kind             ; :running | :blocked | :parked | :halted\ndocs/design/yin.vm.semantic.continuation.md:445:Fork roots of every kind and all children carry nil. Exclusive running, blocked\ndocs/design/yin.vm.semantic.continuation.md:1278:| 11 | install, `:running` wire phase (**amended after 6b, synthetic phase**) | row 10's machine with the install entry's phase set to `:running` **by hand** before the lift | as 10 | act, `:install`, child kind `:blocked`, phase `:running` | `'host.mod` | the program is row 10's; the phase is not engine-reachable at a safepoint (see below) |\ndocs/design/yin.vm.semantic.continuation.md:1296:The running child is an engine state at a fuel boundary; the parked child is blocked at a parking boundary. `advance-install`\ndocs/design/yin.vm.semantic.continuation.md:1323:Historical phase-6 refusal rows (superseded by the completed carrier): `:yin.k/not-quiescent` (`a-nonempty-ready-queue-is-not-quiescent`,\ndocs/design/yin.vm.semantic.continuation.md:1762:2. **Kind.** `:running` when `:control` is set; else `:parked` when the value is a parked continuation the parked table holds; else `:blocked` when the wait set or the ready queue is non-empty; else `:halted` with empty wait set and queue; anything else is `:yin.k/non-portable :inconsistent-state` (unreachable by construction).\ndocs/design/yin.vm.semantic.continuation.md:1817:    running/blocked/parked roots, checks every retained write of the tree against\ndocs/design/yin.vm.semantic.continuation.md:1917:| pendings and install records | `check-pendings!` | the task's role slot equals its position (`:root`/`:child`); every `:install` pending names a carried install row; kind consistency (`:halted` has no waits, `:blocked` has waits, `:parked` names a key of its parked table); then every install record by `check-install!` (§5.2: phase ∈ `#{:running :parked}`, the retained response and image contract, response `:yin.link/id` equals non-nil parent, manifest-named derivation record hashes correctly and connects the manifest tree to the image A, the child `:blocked`) | `:role`, `:incomplete-install`, `:kind`, `:parked-id`, `:install-phase`, `:install-response`, `:install-link-id`, `:install-image`, `:install-child`, all `:yin.k/undecodable` |\ndocs/design/yin.vm.semantic.continuation.md:2024:After the sweep, resume at most one queued entry. Do not immediately run the resumed activation in that invocation. A running child retains phase `:running`; blocked children retain `:parked`; halted children complete installation as today.\ndocs/design/yin.vm.semantic.continuation.md:2234:   `a-nonempty-ready-queue-is-not-quiescent`, ported.\ndocs/design/yin.vm.semantic.continuation.md:2432:3. **Task-product kinds.** Retain running-only, active-plus-waits, active-plus-ready, blocked-plus-ready and halted-plus-ready cases. Add halted-plus-outstanding-wait with empty queue: pin the existing blocked normalization and dropped result separately. Retain invalid run counts, illegal result/parked-id and empty-blocked cases.\ndocs/design/yin.vm.semantic.continuation.md:2866:| B1 | §5.2 rows 10-12, the install paragraph; §8.2 item 3 | row 10 is child `:blocked`, phase `:parked`; row 11 is the `:running` wire phase set by hand on row 10's machine; the lower's install contract (phase set, response and image, child `:blocked`) is stated | `advance-install` retains a blocked child at `:parked` and links a halted or parked one in the same sweep; the promised states were unreachable |\n","exit_code":0,"status":"completed"}}
{"type":"item.started","item":{"id":"item_118","type":"command_execution","command":"/bin/zsh -lc \"sed -n '485,509p' docs/design/yin.vm.semantic.continuation.md; sed -n '604,632p' docs/design/yin.vm.semantic.continuation.md; sed -n '1293,1312p' docs/design/yin.vm.semantic.continuation.md; sed -n '1754,1775p' docs/design/yin.vm.semantic.continuation.md; sed -n '1907,1923p' docs/design/yin.vm.semantic.continuation.md; tail -3 target/6da/r2-focused-b.log\"","aggregated_output":"","exit_code":null,"status":"in_progress"}}
{"type":"item.completed","item":{"id":"item_118","type":"command_execution","command":"/bin/zsh -lc \"sed -n '485,509p' docs/design/yin.vm.semantic.continuation.md; sed -n '604,632p' docs/design/yin.vm.semantic.continuation.md; sed -n '1293,1312p' docs/design/yin.vm.semantic.continuation.md; sed -n '1754,1775p' docs/design/yin.vm.semantic.continuation.md; sed -n '1907,1923p' docs/design/yin.vm.semantic.continuation.md; tail -3 target/6da/r2-focused-b.log\"","aggregated_output":"```clojure\n(frame/defect frame code context task)\n;; frame   : a decoded canonical frame (§1.2), any shape (the rules judge it)\n;; code    : {A vector}, every vector already code/well-formed? (step 4 of the carrier ran)\n;; context : :wait | :captured | :parked | :running | :ready\n;; task    : decoded task context, plain data, no engine:\n;;           {:parked-key P-or-nil                 ; the parked-table key this frame sits under (:parked only)\n;;            :ffi-call-ids #{…}                   ; call ids of the task's live :ffi and :ffi-request pendings\n;;            :free-env {sym V …}}                 ; the root's free environment, decoded\n;; => nil, or {:yin.k/kind k :yin.k/path p …}\n\n(frame/task-defect task)\n;; the once-per-body rule X1 over the decoded task context (its :free-env);\n;; run before any frame of the body; => nil or {:yin.k/kind k :yin.k/path p …}\n```\n\nNamespace `yin.vm.semantic.frame`, file\n`src/cljc/yin/vm/semantic/frame.cljc`, requiring only\n`yin.vm.semantic.code`, `.analysis`, `yin.vm.debruijn`\n(`resolve-name`, for the chain of rule E2) and `yin.vm`\n(`reserved-name?`). It knows no kernel and reads no engine: `task` is\ndecoded from the rows (the parked table's key, the pendings' call ids,\nthe root's `free-env`), never from a running machine. A frame a stack\nkernel lifted and one the register evaluator lifted are judged by the\nsame function on the same inputs.\nQ1 and Q2 receive the completion descriptor through the validation context; they do not fabricate a pending field on the delivery frame. Ready FFI descriptors contribute their call IDs to task context alongside outstanding FFI waits, so parked FFI records remain valid while their response or sent-request outcome is queued.\n\n\n`window-defect` is parameterised by the wanted set: `saved(pc, rd)` for act/return, `live(pc)` for run. A run has no window-self analogue.\n\nValidate every task context first; then judge outstanding waits in `:wait`, active run states in `:running`, ready delivery states in `:ready`, parked states in `:parked`, and reified states in `:captured`. Ready descriptors receive completed-operation validation separately from pending validation. FFI call IDs are collected from outstanding waits and completed outcomes.\n\n### 3.3 Where and when the validator runs\n\n**DECIDED** (carrier order kept: draft §8, step 7 after step 6; the\nreview's ruling). On **lower**: gate (1), structure (2), graph (3),\nhashes (4), canonical form (5), canonical numbering (6), **frames (7)**,\npending and operations (8), dependency closure (9), custody (10),\ncomposition (11), restore (12). In step 7 the body's decoded task\ncontext is judged first by `frame/task-defect` (X1), then every `:act`,\n`:tail`, `:kframe`, `:reified` and parked-table state is decoded and\njudged by `frame/defect` with its context and that task context; a defect\nis `:yin.k/undecodable` with the rule's kind and the row path. A\nfirst-defect test therefore sees a numbering defect\n(`:noncanonical-cursor-cells`) before a frame defect on a body that has both,\nand §8's acceptance items say so. On **lift**: the same function runs\nover every assembled frame before any row is emitted; a frame the\nevaluator itself minted that fails is `:yin.k/non-portable`\n`:inconsistent-state`. The harness runs it over every frame a layout\nreconstructs.\n\n---\n\n## 4. Layouts: reconstructing the canonical frame\n**Amended after 6b (2026-10-13), rows 10-12 and the install contract\n(B1).** The earlier text promised a child \"`:blocked`, phase `:running`\"\n(row 10) and a child \"executing `:park`, kind `:parked`\" (row 11).\nThe running child is an engine state at a fuel boundary; the parked child is blocked at a parking boundary. `advance-install`\n(`engine.cljc:1421-1454`) runs the child inside the sweep and then\nrecords it: a **blocked** child is retained at phase **`:parked`**\n(`:1444-1446`); a **halted** child goes straight to `link-install` in the\nsame sweep (`:1447-1452`), so it is never retained; and a child that\nexecutes `:park` is `:halted?` with a parked value, so it too goes to\n`link-install`, which completes the install if the exports are already\ndefined and otherwise refuses it `:export-missing`. Phase `:running` is\nassigned only in the `:else` arm, within one sweep, and is overwritten\nbefore any safepoint. So: row 10 is the engine's real state (child\n`:blocked`, phase `:parked`); row 11 exercises the `:running` **wire\nphase**, which the codec accepts (`install-node` admits `#{:running\n:parked}` on lift and `check-install!` on lower) and the harness\nconstructs by hand on row 10's machine (`installing % false :running`,\n`safepoint_harness_test.cljc:342`); row 12 is row 10's child under tail\ndelivery. No row promises an executable kind-`:parked` install child on\nthe current engine (owner question §11 Q1). **The install validation\nretained. The holder retains serve answers by `[task-path resource-id]`;\nencode uses those answers without serving externally.\n\nThe merged order is:\n\n**Amended 2026-10-16 (any-pc, owner invariant 2026-10-17)**\n\n1. **Holds.** Refuse `:yin.k/non-portable :reason-mismatch` on an observe wait, held entry, unminted cursor, pending close or link request without its cursor. These are driver-owned incomplete transitions. Their completion can depend on external acknowledgement or backpressure; there is no one-cycle resolution guarantee. There is no ready-queue quiescence refusal: completed outcomes travel in order.\n2. **Kind.** `:running` when `:control` is set; else `:parked` when the value is a parked continuation the parked table holds; else `:blocked` when the wait set or the ready queue is non-empty; else `:halted` with empty wait set and queue; anything else is `:yin.k/non-portable :inconsistent-state` (unreachable by construction).\n3. **Free environment** (§6.3): the option, else the kernel field, else\n   `:missing-free-env`.\n4. **The walk.** The active run state with its window trimmed to `L(pc)`, waits (state and pending), ordered ready outcomes, the parked table, the whole\n   store, the result (halted only), install children (each a recursive\n   `lift-task*` in the child role with its own accumulator), then the\n   module stores by reachability. Every value is classified `[:lit x]`,\n   `[:row n]` or `[:cursor-cell source]`; references are authenticated\n   against the kernel's resource table before encoding\n   (`:forged-resource-reference`), a foreign-owned value is\n   `:foreign-value`, a heap cell `:cell`, a host object `:host-object`.\n   The walk records every **segment** reached and every **context**: a\n   closure's `(A, entry, E)`, an `act`'s or `run`'s `(A, pc, E)`, a return frame's\n   `(A, pc, E)`. A `tail` state contributes its `K` frames' contexts and\n**each over the whole task tree (root and every install child, pre-order)\nbefore the next**, then custody **once for the whole tree**, and\n**every one of them before the first `attach!`**; a defect in a child's\nlater stage therefore cannot be masked by the root's earlier one, and\nzero streams are attached on any refusal (codex F1, F2, F4, F7; mutants\nthat attach early are killed by the attach-count law):\n\n| Stage | Function | Checks, in order | Refusal |\n|---|---|---|---|\n| stores | `check-stores!` | no key of the root store or of any module store is a reserved name (`vm/reserved-name?`), refused here rather than by restore's `store-put` | `:yin.k/undecodable :reserved-name` (`:yin.k/role :store-key`) |\n| pendings and install records | `check-pendings!` | the task's role slot equals its position (`:root`/`:child`); every `:install` pending names a carried install row; kind consistency (`:halted` has no waits, `:blocked` has waits, `:parked` names a key of its parked table); then every install record by `check-install!` (§5.2: phase ∈ `#{:running :parked}`, the retained response and image contract, response `:yin.link/id` equals non-nil parent, manifest-named derivation record hashes correctly and connects the manifest tree to the image A, the child `:blocked`) | `:role`, `:incomplete-install`, `:kind`, `:parked-id`, `:install-phase`, `:install-response`, `:install-link-id`, `:install-image`, `:install-child`, all `:yin.k/undecodable` |\n| dependencies | `check-dependencies!` | `requires` is a map whose `:yin.k/segments` equals the key set of `code` (`:requires`); every segment has a non-empty `:yin.k/trees` entry; every `store-of` of every `:closure` and `:env` row of **this task** (children excluded, each checked in its own stage pass) names one of this task's `:module-store` rows (§2.6), so a parent's or sibling's store of the same key cannot answer (codex F7, F8); every vector attaches in the receiving kernel under its A (`attaches?`: `module/attach-module` into a throwaway copy, the result discarded) (`:segment`); every `:closure` row names a `:closure` tuple of its vector at its entry (`:closure-origin`) with the same binders (`:closure-binders`); every `:prim` names a primitive the receiver holds | `:yin.k/undecodable :requires`, `:yin.k/unsatisfied` with `:yin.k/trees` or **`:yin.k/stores`** (`:yin.k/discovery :incomplete`), `:yin.k/undecodable :segment`, `:closure-origin`, `:closure-binders`, `:yin.k/unsatisfied {:yin.k/name p}` |\n| custody | `check-custody!` | `custody-baseline` over the tree; fork refused under `:exclusive`; halted exclusive needs no grant; blocked/parked exclusive validates grant evidence, pack checkpoint, binding, lease/holder, arbitration, epoch, live tenure and input prefix, then protection in both directions and op-id presence against enrollment; `:fenced` skips grant/protection | grammar's `:yin.k/undecodable` kinds; `:yin.k/profile-mismatch`, `:yin.k/awaiting-grant`, `:yin.k/not-holder`, `:yin.k/unsatisfied` |\n| modules | `check-modules!` | Whole-tree module address and used host-export profile equality; carried install children require receiver admission; after custody, before attach | `:yin.k/unsatisfied :module-pin-mismatch`, `:host-export-mismatch`, or collected missing with `:yin.k/discovery :complete` |\n\n**Amended 2026-10-16 (module-pins, R4).** After custody validation and\nbefore attachment, every carried install child must have its manifest\nTesting yin.vm.semantic.frame-test\n\nTesting yin.vm.semantic.safepoint-harness-test\n","exit_code":0,"status":"completed"}}
