{"type":"item.completed","item":{"id":"item_119","type":"command_execution","command":"/bin/zsh -lc \"sed -n '263,305p' /Users/sto/workspace/datomworld/collab/1792145566000-architect-6d-plan-v21.report.md; sed -n '1996,2046p' docs/design/yin.vm.semantic.continuation.md; sed -n '2350,2373p' test/yin/vm/semantic/safepoint_harness_test.cljc; rg -n 'defn.' src/cljc/yin/vm/ucf/rows.cljc | tail -10\"","aggregated_output":"\n**Change:** Consensus P2-8 supplies an explicit exception-state channel; P1-2 moves fencing into 6d-a while retaining lifecycle tests in 6d-b.\n\n### 3.4 Fuel and budget propagation\n\n**Replaces v2 §3.4 completely.**\n\n**`yin.vm.semantic/run-fuel [machine n]`**, public, with positive exact integer `n`.\n\nOne invocation performs:\n\n1. Closed-gate check.\n2. Exactly one raw budgeted action:\n   - If control is present, `vm-hot` with fuel `n`.\n   - Otherwise, one budgeted scheduler round.\n3. If the result is blocked and an explicit bridge is installed, at most one `ffi/bridge-step`.\n4. Return that resulting machine immediately.\n\nThe implementation does **not** wrap the raw action in unchanged `ffi/maybe-run`. A handled response or malformed-request diagnostic does not restart the runner or bridge inside the same invocation. The next caller invocation resumes progress.\n\nThe bounded bridge helper may be private to the semantic runner or a bounded variant beside `ffi/maybe-run`; its contract is the four steps above. Existing unrestricted `vm/run` bridge behavior remains unchanged for live machines.\n\n**Budgeted scheduler round.**\n\nPropagate the budget through `check-wait-set`, `poll-links`, `advance-installs` and `advance-install`. Each visited child is invoked once through `run-fuel child n`; nested children use the same rule. Preserve existing gate stamping and the prohibition on running children under closed gates.\n\nAfter the sweep, resume at most one queued entry. Do not immediately run the resumed activation in that invocation. A running child retains phase `:running`; blocked children retain `:parked`; halted children complete installation as today.\n\nThe dispatch tests **control presence**, not merely `engine/active-continuation?`: the latter only tests blocked/halted flags and can classify a control-less ingress-ready machine as active. Therefore no `run-fuel` path falls through `vm-hot` into its unbudgeted scheduler fallback. A quiescent control-less machine takes the budgeted no-work round and returns.\n\n**Per-tree bound.**\n\nEach task visited during the invocation receives at most one budgeted action and at most one bridge step. Each task executes at most `n` guest instructions. For `t` distinct tasks visited during the invocation, including children created during the round, the instruction bound is `n × t`. No task is revisited with a fresh budget inside that invocation.\n\n**The honest guarantee**, copied verbatim into the documents:\n\n> Fuel counts completed guest instructions. One `run-fuel` invocation executes at most `n` instructions per visited task, at most one scheduler round per visited inactive task, and at most one bridge step per visited task. A bridge result never restarts execution inside that invocation. No wall-clock bound is claimed for an instruction, host function, stream constructor, variable resolution, bridge step or scheduler sweep. The VM has no clock and converts no time to instructions; `dao.lease` owns liveness and the composition chooses `n`.\n\n`vm/step` keeps its telemetry behavior. `run-fuel` adds no per-fuel snapshot; existing park, resume and bridge telemetry remains.\n\nRunning install children use the same carrier and receiver-admission checks as other tasks. The backends continue to refuse install children.\n\n**Change:** Consensus P1-1 bounds bridge execution; glm’s inactive-predicate omission is closed explicitly.\nEvery kind restores slot 18 in order. Resolve the ready state and completion descriptor, reconstruct the engine entry described in §3.1, then restore its value, status, refusal and resource updates. Update keys map through the slot-9 C→fresh-resource-key map; update bodies come from the ready row, not from slot 9.\n\nNo completed operation is polled or reissued by lower. A completed FFI request append resumes through the existing response-wait transition. Link/install completion restores without resurrecting retired pending resources.\n\nA fenced restore retains ready entries in `:yin.k/recovery-ready`, alongside recovery waits and parked records, and exposes an empty scheduler queue. Running control remains available for byte-identical relift, protected by the 6d-a closed-gate guard.\n\n\n### 7.4 Fuel\n\n**`yin.vm.semantic/run-fuel [machine n]`**, public, with positive exact integer `n`.\n\nOne invocation performs:\n\n1. Closed-gate check.\n2. Exactly one raw budgeted action:\n   - If control is present, `vm-hot` with fuel `n`.\n   - Otherwise, one budgeted scheduler round.\n3. If the result is blocked and an explicit bridge is installed, at most one `ffi/bridge-step`.\n4. Return that resulting machine immediately.\n\nThe implementation does **not** wrap the raw action in unchanged `ffi/maybe-run`. A handled response or malformed-request diagnostic does not restart the runner or bridge inside the same invocation. The next caller invocation resumes progress.\n\nThe bounded bridge helper may be private to the semantic runner or a bounded variant beside `ffi/maybe-run`; its contract is the four steps above. Existing unrestricted `vm/run` bridge behavior remains unchanged for live machines.\n\n**Budgeted scheduler round.**\n\nPropagate the budget through `check-wait-set`, `poll-links`, `advance-installs` and `advance-install`. Each visited child is invoked once through `run-fuel child n`; nested children use the same rule. Preserve existing gate stamping and the prohibition on running children under closed gates.\n\nAfter the sweep, resume at most one queued entry. Do not immediately run the resumed activation in that invocation. A running child retains phase `:running`; blocked children retain `:parked`; halted children complete installation as today.\n\nThe dispatch tests **control presence**, not merely `engine/active-continuation?`: the latter only tests blocked/halted flags and can classify a control-less ingress-ready machine as active. Therefore no `run-fuel` path falls through `vm-hot` into its unbudgeted scheduler fallback. A quiescent control-less machine takes the budgeted no-work round and returns.\n\n**Per-tree bound.**\n\nEach task visited during the invocation receives at most one budgeted action and at most one bridge step. Each task executes at most `n` guest instructions. For `t` distinct tasks visited during the invocation, including children created during the round, the instruction bound is `n × t`. No task is revisited with a fresh budget inside that invocation.\n\n**The honest guarantee**, copied verbatim into the documents:\n\n> Fuel counts completed guest instructions. One `run-fuel` invocation executes at most `n` instructions per visited task, at most one scheduler round per visited inactive task, and at most one bridge step per visited task. A bridge result never restarts execution inside that invocation. No wall-clock bound is claimed for an instruction, host function, stream constructor, variable resolution, bridge step or scheduler sweep. The VM has no clock and converts no time to instructions; `dao.lease` owns liveness and the composition chooses `n`.\n\n`vm/step` keeps its telemetry behavior. `run-fuel` adds no per-fuel snapshot; existing park, resume and bridge telemetry remains.\n\nRunning install children use the same carrier and receiver-admission checks as other tasks. The backends continue to refuse install children.\n\n\n## 8. Slices, gates, entry conditions\n\nVerification follows `docs/agents/build-n-test.md`: G0 per iteration on\nthe JVM, G1 `bb test:sub yin.vm` on three hosts, G2 `bb test:changed`,\nG3 on master.\n\n         (when execution\n           (doseq [target (if (and (= :sample execution) (not (contains? #{1 20} row)))\n                            (sort (set (remove nil? (vals (structural-sample @points))))) measured)\n                   :when (not (:excluded? (nth @points target)))]\n             (let [i (atom -1)\n                   replay (with-redefs [vm/run #(fuel-drive % (fn [m]\n                                                                (if (= target (swap! i inc))\n                                                                  (direct-transfer m) m)))]\n                            (reference (build)))]\n               (is (= expected replay) (str \"isolated law 1 \" [row segment target])))))\n         {:row row :segment segment :measured (count measured)\n          :samples (structural-sample @points)\n          :coverage (boundary-coverage @points)\n          :excluded-leading (mapv #(select-keys % [:pc :obligations]) excluded)\n          :park (count (filter #(= :parked (:stop %)) @points))\n          :halt (count (filter #(= :halted (:stop %)) @points))})) cases)))\n\n\n(deftest sampled-returned-boundaries\n  (let [cases (filterv #(or (= :bare (second %)) (= 20 (first %))) (matrix-cases))\n        counts (check-returned-boundaries cases :sample)]\n    (is (= 23 (count counts)))\n    (is (every? pos? (map :measured counts)))\n    (println \"6d-a quick boundary counts JVM:\" (pr-str counts))))\n2023:(defn- check-modules!\n2052:(defn- check-closure!\n2067:(defn- check-dependencies!\n2100:(defn- accept-grant!\n2180:(defn- check-custody!\n2199:(defn- with-custody\n2225:(defn- attach-streams!\n2238:(defn- spawn-child\n2261:(defn- restore-task\n2456:(defn lower-task\n","exit_code":0,"status":"completed"}}
{"type":"item.started","item":{"id":"item_120","type":"command_execution","command":"/bin/zsh -lc \"python3 - <<'PY'\np='docs/design/yin.vm.semantic.continuation.md';s=open(p).read();s=s.replace('Two closed state shapes and one closed delivery record:','Three closed state shapes and one closed delivery record:')\ns=s.replace('frames           ; crefs to :wait rows, in wait order     (:blocked, :parked)','frames           ; crefs to :wait rows, in wait order     (:running, :blocked, :parked)')\ns=s.replace('''\"'`:tail`, `:kframe`, `:reified` and parked-table state is decoded and'\"''','''\"'`:tail`, `:run`, `:kframe`, `:reified`, ready delivery and parked-table state is decoded and'\"''')\ns=s.replace('the task\\\\'s live :ffi and :ffi-request pendings','the task\\\\'s outstanding and completed FFI call ids')\ns=s.replace('''kind consistency (\"'`:halted` has no waits, `:blocked` has waits, `:parked` names a key of its parked table); then every install record'\"''','''kind consistency (the complete §2.6 product table: a single run for \"'`:running`, waits or ready for `:blocked`, neither for `:halted`, a held key for `:parked`); completed-outcome status/refusal checks and shape-only IDs at slot 18; then every install record'\"''')\ns=s.replace('''the child \"'`:blocked`)'\"''','''child kind \"'`:blocked` at phase `:parked`, `:running` at phase `:running`)'\"''')\ns=s.replace('''blocked/parked exclusive validates grant''','''running/blocked/parked exclusive validates grant''')\ns=s.replace('''The receiver's registry is kept as given.''','''The receiver's registry pins and slices are kept as given. Its task-local lowered bindings are recreated through \"'`engine/receive-module` after the carried images and stores, so they name the restored task'\"'s code coordinates and carried live stores win.''')\ns=s.replace('''The merged order is:\\\\n''','''Before entering handles in the external serving table, \"'`lift-task*` runs with temporary plain-data identities to check portability, frames and conservative discharge. This preflight does not call the composition'\"'s \"'`serve!` or `:serve-keyed`. A discharge refusal therefore serves zero handles. `discharge!` and its edge-reachability conservatism are unchanged.'\"\\\\n\\\\nThe merged order is:\\\\n''',1)\ns=s.replace('''| 11 | install, \"'`:running` wire phase (**amended after 6b, synthetic phase**) | row 10'\"'s machine with the install entry's phase set to \"'`:running` **by hand** before the lift | as 10 | act, `:install`, child kind `:blocked`, phase `:running` | `'\"'host.mod\"'` | the program is row 10'\"'s; the phase is not engine-reachable at a safepoint (see below) |''','''| 11 | install at a running child's fuel boundary | row 10's child is fed and advanced by \"'`run-fuel 1`; its active control is carried | as 10 | act, `:install`, child kind `:running`, phase `:running` | `'\"'host.mod\"'` | the running child is obtained by execution |'\"''')\na=s.index('Phase \"'`:running` is'\"\\\\nassigned only in the \"'`:else` arm'\"');b=s.index('No row promises an executable',a)\ns=s[:a]+'''**Amended 2026-10-16 (any-pc, owner invariant 2026-10-17).** A budgeted sweep can retain a child with active control at phase \"'`:running`. Row 11 now obtains that state by real execution. The lower requires a `:running` child at phase `:running` and a `:blocked` child at phase `:parked`. Row 12 is row 10'\"'s child under tail delivery. '''+s[b:]\ns=s.replace('''at reachable non-tail PCs and \"'`set(uses(p)) = L(p)`'\"''','''at reachable non-tail PCs except the four enumerated dead ambient operand PCs in §8.6 item 9, and \"'`set(uses(p)) = L(p)`'\"''')\nopen(p,'w').write(s)\nPY\n\"","aggregated_output":"","exit_code":null,"status":"in_progress"}}
