{"type":"item.started","item":{"id":"item_132","type":"command_execution","command":"/bin/zsh -lc \"rg -n 'Stage-local execution returns|Restore the ready queue in carried order|Each ready entry contributes|Check ordered region length and contents' docs/design/yin.vm.semantic.continuation.md; rg -n 'All three|All.*two|two state|only.*act|only.*tail|three kinds|:blocked.*:parked.*:halted|:wait.*:captured.*:parked' docs/design/yin.vm.semantic.continuation.md docs/design/yin.vm.ucf-transport-tuples.md docs/design/yin.vm.semantic.md > target/6da/r2-exhaustive-lists.txt; cat target/6da/r2-exhaustive-lists.txt | head -25; sed -n '1938,1996p' docs/design/yin.vm.semantic.continuation.md; sed -n '890,905p' docs/design/yin.vm.ucf-transport-tuples.md\"","aggregated_output":"","exit_code":null,"status":"in_progress"}}
{"type":"item.completed","item":{"id":"item_132","type":"command_execution","command":"/bin/zsh -lc \"rg -n 'Stage-local execution returns|Restore the ready queue in carried order|Each ready entry contributes|Check ordered region length and contents' docs/design/yin.vm.semantic.continuation.md; rg -n 'All three|All.*two|two state|only.*act|only.*tail|three kinds|:blocked.*:parked.*:halted|:wait.*:captured.*:parked' docs/design/yin.vm.semantic.continuation.md docs/design/yin.vm.ucf-transport-tuples.md docs/design/yin.vm.semantic.md > target/6da/r2-exhaustive-lists.txt; cat target/6da/r2-exhaustive-lists.txt | head -25; sed -n '1938,1996p' docs/design/yin.vm.semantic.continuation.md; sed -n '890,905p' docs/design/yin.vm.ucf-transport-tuples.md\"","aggregated_output":"1829:Each ready entry contributes its delivery state, completed descriptor, lifted outcome and optional refusal, and explicit resource-update bodies. Completed descriptors do not re-enter outstanding-pending validation.\ndocs/design/yin.vm.ucf-transport-tuples.md:430:   kind             ; :blocked | :parked | :halted\ndocs/design/yin.vm.ucf-transport-tuples.md:911:the three kinds this carrier adds to UCF §7.5.4's set: `:byte-string`,\ndocs/design/yin.vm.semantic.md:380:`ret` frame corresponds only to a suspended caller activation. The\ndocs/design/yin.vm.semantic.md:1023:only in facts A omits, same A). Pinned checksums are regenerated, once\ndocs/design/yin.vm.semantic.md:1078:1. **Identity.** Amend the A-only identity contracts. **Complete**\ndocs/design/yin.vm.semantic.continuation.md:257:The two delivery states of §1.1 are the states at which the evaluator parks by itself. They are special cases of its general state between any two instructions, `⟨A, pc, W↾L(pc), E, K⟩`, which `vm-hot` materializes whenever fuel runs out (`semantic.cljc:142-143`) and which the carrier expresses as the `run` state of §1.2. A step is atomic: effects are observed only inside a step or inside the scheduler's sweep, so no state between steps holds a half-issued effect; atomicity of a step is not transactionality of the outside world (an append performed before a host exception is not undone). A task is a **product**: at most one active activation (the `run`), its ordered pending waits, its ordered completed wakes (the ready queue: a woken wait with the value, status and cursor update its effect produced, carried by the `:ready` row of §2.3), its parked table, and its stores. The scheduler constructs every combination: resuming one of several woken waits leaves the others queued and the unresolved ones pending (`engine.cljc:2294-2312`, `:2305`). Every such state is **representable**. The lift refuses only what is not **portable** (a value with no wire form), not **satisfied** (code or dependencies the receiver lacks), or a **hold** (a driver-internal observation in flight: §7.1 step 1), never a pc. The static correspondence of §4 holds at every pc of a body: distinct virtuals in `L(p) ∪ def(p)` hold distinct physical registers (`derive/allocation`), and the stack kernel's operand region at A pc `p` is `stack-layout(p) ++ uses(p)` above a dead prefix (§4.3); both are checks (§5.6), not theorems. A root whose task has an active activation has kind `:running` (§2.6) and is a custody subject like a blocked or parked root (§7.3).\ndocs/design/yin.vm.semantic.continuation.md:359:the frozen §4.1 table's two state columns. The 4b evaluator's in-VM\ndocs/design/yin.vm.semantic.continuation.md:420:   kind             ; :running | :blocked | :parked | :halted\ndocs/design/yin.vm.semantic.continuation.md:489:;; context : :wait | :captured | :parked | :running | :ready\ndocs/design/yin.vm.semantic.continuation.md:539:**The current activation (`act` only; `tail` and `run` skip A1-A6).**\ndocs/design/yin.vm.semantic.continuation.md:581:| P1 | `:wait` requires pending; `:captured`, `:parked`, `:running`, `:ready` require pending absent. Run is admitted only in `:running`; `:ready` admits only act/tail. | `:pending-presence` |\ndocs/design/yin.vm.semantic.continuation.md:602:| Q5 | Every present completed operation ID passes shape-only validation. | `:malformed-op-id`, `:inexact` |\ndocs/design/yin.vm.semantic.continuation.md:1911:| pendings and install records | `check-pendings!` | the task's role slot equals its position (`:root`/`:child`); every `:install` pending names a carried install row; kind consistency (the complete §2.6 product table: a single run for `:running`, waits or ready for `:blocked`, neither for `:halted`, a held key for `:parked`); completed-outcome status/refusal checks and shape-only IDs at slot 18; then every install record by `check-install!` (§5.2: phase ∈ `#{:running :parked}`, the retained response and image contract, response `:yin.link/id` equals non-nil parent, manifest-named derivation record hashes correctly and connects the manifest tree to the image A, child kind `:blocked` at phase `:parked`, `:running` at phase `:running`) | `:role`, `:incomplete-install`, `:kind`, `:parked-id`, `:install-phase`, `:install-response`, `:install-link-id`, `:install-image`, `:install-child`, all `:yin.k/undecodable` |\ndocs/design/yin.vm.semantic.continuation.md:2020:The dispatch tests **control presence**, not merely `engine/active-continuation?`: the latter only tests blocked/halted flags and can classify a control-less ingress-ready machine as active. Therefore no `run-fuel` path falls through `vm-hot` into its unbudgeted scheduler fallback. A quiescent control-less machine takes the budgeted no-work round and returns.\ndocs/design/yin.vm.semantic.continuation.md:2426:3. **Task-product kinds.** Retain running-only, active-plus-waits, active-plus-ready, blocked-plus-ready and halted-plus-ready cases. Add halted-plus-outstanding-wait with empty queue: pin the existing blocked normalization and dropped result separately. Retain invalid run counts, illegal result/parked-id and empty-blocked cases.\ndocs/design/yin.vm.semantic.continuation.md:2442:11. **Bounded bridge execution.** A program repeatedly making bridge-served FFI calls returns from every `run-fuel` invocation. Each invocation executes at most one raw action and one bridge step. Repeated invocations reach the reference result. Diagnostic-only bridge input also returns after one step. Pin control-less ingress-ready dispatch to the budgeted round. For a pure active computation lasting at least `n` instructions, compare with `n` single-instruction steps; an earlier park/halt ends the comparison there.\ndocs/design/yin.vm.semantic.continuation.md:2846:Frozen §2.4 delivery shapes against the 4b branch; frozen §4.1 two state\ndocs/design/yin.vm.semantic.continuation.md:2922:| P1 | `:wait` requires pending; `:captured`, `:parked`, `:running`, `:ready` require pending absent. Run is admitted only in `:running`; `:ready` admits only act/tail. | `:pending-presence` |\nreceiver's own aliases and no source-local segment number travels; fresh\nresource keys per stream identity and per cursor cell; values re-sealed\nunder the receiver's owner; waits in `lower-frame!`'s entry shapes, a\n`tail` with `{:deliver :return}` and no window, env or pc; parked records\nwith a cycle guard; the store through `engine/store-put`; module stores;\ninstall children spawned by the engine's spawn discipline and then\nrestored recursively (the spawn's initial control is replaced, no\n`vm/run`); the free environment as both `:env` and `:free-env`; the id\ncounter `max(local, carried)` for ordinary resume. Restore meets no carrier\ndefect, by\nconstruction of the stages above. `check-modules!` checks bindings over the\nwhole tree after custody and before attachment: unequal held addresses or\nprofiles refuse terminally as `:module-pin-mismatch` or `:host-export-mismatch`;\nabsent bindings, absent exports and unadmitted install children are collected\nin one `:yin.k/unsatisfied` with `:yin.k/discovery :complete` and\n`:yin.k/missing {:yin.k/modules … :yin.k/host-exports …}` (only nonempty keys).\nThe receiver's registry pins and slices are kept as given. Its task-local lowered bindings are recreated through `engine/receive-module` after the carried images and stores, so they name the restored task's code coordinates and carried live stores win. The kinds `:role :custody :incomplete-install\n:kind :parked-id :requires :segment :install-phase :install-response\n:install-child :closure-origin :closure-binders` and the `:yin.k/stores`\ncensus are the engineer's and the fix rounds' naming; the earlier text\nnamed none of them (deviation 9, accepted with the requirement that every\ndefect be a named transport outcome before attachment).\n\n**Amended after 7 (2026-10-14)** — Reason: fenced lowering is administrative recovery, not grant admission.\nWith `:fenced true`, every task is gated `:exporting`; waits move to\n`:yin.k/recovery-waits`, every parked record to `:yin.k/recovery-parked`,\nand the id counter is exactly the carried value. Resource keys are\nassociated with their cursor-cell ids in `:yin.k/recovery-cell-ids`.\nChild spawning temporarily disables `:make-stream`, initializes nothing\nand restores the constructor afterward. `holder.export/rehydrate-fenced`\nchecks the recovery header and local state before lower, moves waits and\nparked records into the retained export record, and proves byte-identical\nre-emission. It restores no tenure or runnable gate; recovered abort refuses.\nA grant's `:checkpoint` names the pack address, never the root id.\n\n---\n\n**Amended 2026-10-16 (any-pc, owner invariant 2026-10-17)**\n\nA running task restores:\n\n```clojure\n{:control {:segment local :pc pc}\n :window W\n :env E\n :k (when (seq K) K)\n :halted? false\n :blocked? false\n :value nil\n :wait-set entries}\n```\n\nEvery kind restores slot 18 in order. Resolve the ready state and completion descriptor, reconstruct the engine entry described in §3.1, then restore its value, status, refusal and resource updates. Update keys map through the slot-9 C→fresh-resource-key map; update bodies come from the ready row, not from slot 9.\n\nNo completed operation is polled or reissued by lower. A completed FFI request append resumes through the existing response-wait transition. Link/install completion restores without resurrecting retired pending resources.\n\nA fenced restore retains ready entries in `:yin.k/recovery-ready`, alongside recovery waits and parked records, and exposes an empty scheduler queue. Running control remains available for byte-identical relift, protected by the 6d-a closed-gate guard.\n\n\nrows (continuation §11 Q2), and `requires` beyond segments, trees and\nprimitives (modules, streams, cursor profiles) is not evaluated on\nlower; free names are discharged at lift only (continuation §7.1).\nRefusals are thrown `ex-info` with `:yin.k/status` and a `:yin.k/kind`.\n11. **Composition.** Protection, resource, primitive and grant inputs of\n    the receiving composition.\n12. **Restore.** Reconstruct isolated code spaces, fresh values, the\n    isolated store, module-store instances (first link wins), one\n    private resource entry per cursor cell, the parked table, children first\n    (one native task instance **per install entry**, even where two\n    entries share a child row), then waits in order; adopt `max(local,\n    carried)` for the id counter; publish the machine only after every\n    child succeeds; run, poll, mint, append, close or initialize nothing\n    during lower.\n\nDiagnostics use the established families and no new top-level outcome:\n","exit_code":0,"status":"completed"}}
